                <pb facs="0521" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24363.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Monroe to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-15"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 15, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Monroe reports that earthquakes have been continuous in San Jose for the past
                    60 hours. Says there are property losses, but no loss of life, and that there is
                    excitement on all sides.</p>
            </div>
